  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`indexFor`): a rapid or linear record with no A word is refused by name when the operation holds an A that is not 0 (modulo 360). The post does not write the refused move.\n- Before this change, the post read the record as tool angle 0. Since #2386 it then wrote a `G0` / `G1` block with an `A0` word in the middle of the operation. That turn swings the part under the tool.\n- A record with no A word in an upright operation posts as before. A record with no A word after a stated `A0` posts as before.\n- Refusal text: `move in operation <name> states no A angle while the operation holds A<angle> - the post turns A inside an operation only on a move that states its A angle`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Reproduced: on the main post script, the two refusal tests fail (no warning, the move posts). With the fix, they pass.\n- Source reading of the stream: `post::dump` (`crates/post/src/post/mod.rs`, the `(None, None)` arm) gives a record with no angle when the CL move states no axis. Its comment says that such a move \"keeps the modal pose\". A real turn back to upright gets an explicit `A0` (the `(None, Some(_)) if tilted` arm). Thus a record with no A word after a non-zero A is never a stated turn.\n- No generator was found that emits such a record: the CL path attaches the modal axis to each move. The refusal is a guard. It refuses no known legal program.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2473-tormach-a-without-word.md` (refuse, not keep the section angle, and why).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/post/tests/tormach_no_a_word.rs`:\n- `a_rapid_with_no_a_word_in_an_indexed_operation_is_refused`\n- `a_linear_move_with_no_a_word_in_an_indexed_operation_is_refused`\n- `a_stated_turn_to_a0_then_a_move_with_no_a_word_still_posts`\n\n## Gate (local, Windows, debug, -j 6)\n\nThe quick gate selects all 862 steps for a post script change. For that reason I ran the binaries that load `tormach.cps`, one step for each binary:\n\n- `camcraft-post --tests`: all binaries pass (88 test results ok).\n- `camcraft-app`: pass for `conformance`, `first_4axis_part`, `fourth_axis_pose`, `index_swing`, `index_swing_horizontal`, `mcp_rotary_stack`, `post_spindle_rule_all`, `program_units`, `rotary_feed_cap`, `rotary_subplate`, `rotary_subplate_standing`, `setup_mount`, `tilt_a180`, `tormach_end_units`, `tormach_fourth_axis`, `tormach_post`, `tormach_program_end`, `tormach_safe_retract`, `tormach_toolchange_lift`, `tormach_wrapped_a`, `wcs_index`, `wcs_rotation_control`.\n- `camcraft-app microarc_test_part`: `a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a` fails. This is the known main failure #2483. It fails with the same text on the main post script (`wrap_rotary_parallel_microarc4.nc: line count 3246 != 3245`). The new refusal text does not occur in its output.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No recorded `.cl` from a real operation that emits such a record. No generator was found that does.\n- The other `camcraft-app` suites that load Tormach machines (lathe, plasma, probe) were not run. They do not use the A rotary path of `indexFor`.\n- Not run on a PathPilot control.\n- No pixel snapshot changed.\n\nEffort: high (not escalated).\n\nChangelog: Tormach PathPilot post: a move with no A angle inside an operation indexed away from A0 is now refused by name; before, the post turned A back to A0 in the middle of the operation.\n\nFixes #2473\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
